{"reference":"Ecclesiastes 4","book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":4,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Oppression and despair","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Verses 1–3 look directly at oppression: those harmed are pictured weeping without comfort, while power rests with their oppressors. The speaker’s harsh comparisons between the living, the dead, and those not yet born express the extremity of what he has seen; the passage does not offer a quick resolution to such injustice.","verse_refs":["Ecclesiastes 4:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ecclesiastes_004_1d9ff700a7dfc2ede84da674"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}